# Two of vtium's kitty replies keep to the specification's text. A reply's
# message holds only printable characters and spaces, so the reply to a
# composition whose destination frame does not exist ends with no line
# feed. A relative placement that would make a cycle is refused with
# ECYCLE, and a placement that names itself as its parent makes the
# shortest cycle.
#
# References: ADR-1100 D13, D15.
# spec: kitty graphics protocol, "Querying support for protocol features": "The message data will be a ASCII encoded string containing only printable characters and spaces"; "Relative placements": "Terminals are required to reject the creation of a relative placement that would create a cycle", answered with "the ECYCLE error code"
# covers: image.kitty
# covers: image.kitty-relative
size 12 4
send "\e_Ga=T,i=1,p=1,f=24,s=1,v=1,C=1;/wAA\e\\"
send "\e_Ga=c,i=1,r=1,c=5\e\\"
send "\e_Ga=p,i=1,p=1,P=1,Q=1\e\\"
send "\e_Ga=p,i=1,p=2,P=1,Q=1,q=1\e\\"
send "\e_Ga=p,i=1,p=1,P=1,Q=2\e\\"
dump
